course: dictionary
lesson: 12704
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning the writer means. The word dole is a good example. «Dad lost his job, so he is now on the dole.» The words lost his job tell you that dole is about money from the government for people with no work.
explain: «At the party, Gran doled out the cake, one small slice for each child.» Here doled out is a verb. The clues are one small slice for each child: she gave small amounts to several people. Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «Gran gave out small shares to each child» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Dole can also be an old word for a share of food or money given to poor people. You may meet it in older stories. When you see dole, check the clues: is there a job, is the money from the government, or are several people sharing something?
fact: Dole has three main meanings: money from the government for people with no job, a verb meaning to give out small amounts, and an old word for a share of food or money.
fact: «On the dole» is informal, and you will hear it in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: The formal names for this money are «unemployment benefit» and «Jobseeker's Allowance».
fact: «Dole out» means to give out small amounts to several people: «The teacher doled out the paper.»
fact: A «dole queue» is a line of people waiting to collect their dole money.
exercise: «Dad lost his job, so he is now on the dole.» What does on the dole mean? | Working very hard at the office | Sitting in a long queue for a bus | Very happy and rich | * Out of work and getting money from the government
exercise: «Gran doled out sweets to the children, a few each.» What does doled out mean? | * Gave out small amounts to several people | Threw away on the floor | Bought one huge box for one child | Hid in a drawer
exercise: Sam says the dole means a long holiday. Is he right? | No, it is a kind of dog | * No, it is money from the government for people with no job | Yes, a party with cake | Yes, a long holiday by the sea
test: «The teacher doled out the paper, one sheet to each child.» What does doled out mean here? | Lost in the classroom | * Gave out small amounts to several people | Took back from the children | Folded into paper planes
test: What is a formal name for «on the dole» money? | Birthday money | Prize money | * Jobseeker's Allowance | Pocket money
exam: Which clue shows that dole means money from the government in «He was paid the dole after losing his job»? | A happy smile | * after losing his job | The morning sun | A big red car
